the sentencing phase just wrapping up  for the day for the box truck driver who  killed five cyclists in september rather  december near searchlight  45 year old jordan barson admitted he  was under the influence of meth when he  ran into that group on u.s 95.  joe muller in the courtroom today where  relatives and victims  shared their struggles moving on or  trying to without their loved ones  brian it was an emotional day in court  we heard from some of the family members  of those victims and we also heard from  the accused jordan barson  now back in april barson entered a plea  agreement which would reduce  the charges he was facing to two counts  of dui resulting in death  family of some of the victims described  how the sudden deaths of their loved  ones change their lives  the first family member to speak was  donna trauger the wife of tom trauger  she shared how the loss of her husband  haunts her every day  i wasn't prepared when i drove out to  the crash site and saw the letters  hd and ft sprayed on the road  and later learned that these were used  to identify where the head and feet of  the victims lay dead  these words and images haunt me as i lie  in bed at night waiting  praying hoping for sleep to come  at the start of the sentencing hearing  barshen stood up via video and said he  was  sorry and that he is ashamed with  himself he says after he gets out of  prison he wants to share his story and  rehab facilities to prevent another  tragedy  like this now barson faces up to 40  years in prison we  expect to hear from more family members  of those victims tomorrow and sentencing  continues  reporting live in downtown las vegas joe  mohler 8 news now
 

